-- title:
--   Affine output coordinates and sample-table encodings
-- statement:
--   Affine outputs are represented by integer offsets and columns, then serialized as sample-table data. These definitions specify the coordinates, loads, root data, matrix assembly, and output encoding used by the Gaussian preprocessing program. The encoding exposes the concrete integer affine map to the later sample transformation.
